  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target audience is likely individuals who are familiar with Morgan Freeman’s public persona and the historical context of slavery, and who may be susceptible to false equivalences or racist stereotypes. The meme is designed to appeal to viewers who might interpret the juxtaposition of a modern Black celebrity with a historical image of enslaved people as implying a connection or responsibility, thereby reinforcing anti-Black stereotypes. The audience may include those who are not critically aware of the historical and racial dynamics involved, or who are predisposed to racially charged narratives. The meme’s toxicity and harmful intent suggest it is crafted to provoke or entertain through misinformation, targeting communities that may be exposed to or propagate such content online.",
